	<!-- ================================================================
	     COLLECTED DATA (D44/F1108, filled 2026-08-03).

	     This array was EMPTY — i.e. the manifest claimed the app collects
	     nothing — while the app collected location, identity, photos, user
	     content and Sentry diagnostics. Apple cross-checks this file against
	     the App Privacy answers in App Store Connect; "collects nothing" from
	     a location-first social app is the loudest possible mismatch, so this
	     was a submission gate, not a cleanup.

	     Every entry below was verified against code before it was declared:

     * EmailAddress / Name / UserID — Clerk (@clerk/clerk-expo). Email via
       src/components/EmailAuthModal.tsx (email-code sign-in); Apple/Google
       OAuth via src/hooks/useClerkOAuth.ts; displayName/username are rendered
       across the profile/poll surfaces, so they are stored server-side.
     * PreciseLocation — expo-location. Foreground only
       (requestForegroundPermissionsAsync / getCurrentPositionAsync /
       watchPositionAsync in navigation/runtime/MainLaunchCoordinator.tsx and
       providers/AuthProvider.tsx). NO background collection: zero
       requestBackgroundPermissionsAsync / startLocationUpdatesAsync, no
       UIBackgroundModes, no background-location entitlement — see F1106.
     * PhotosorVideos — expo-image-picker uploads on the post-photos and
       edit-profile paths (overlays/PostPhotosFunnelHost.tsx,
       overlays/panels/EditProfilePanel.tsx) plus expo-camera capture.
     * OtherUserContent — posts, polls, poll comments and direct messages.
     * SearchHistory — viewed restaurants/foods are persisted server-side and
       read back (services/search.ts -> POST/GET /history/restaurants/viewed
       and /history/foods/viewed).
     * PurchaseHistory — RevenueCat (react-native-purchases), configured with
       `appUserID: clerkUserId` (services/purchases.ts:85), so it is linked.
     * DeviceID — the Expo push token (providers/AuthProvider.tsx:226) is a
       device-scoped identifier we store against the account.
     * CrashData — Sentry (@sentry/react-native). The ONLY entry with
       Linked=false, and that is a contract the code enforces, not an
       assumption: src/observability/crash-reporting.ts sets
       sendDefaultPii:false, calls Sentry.setUser NOWHERE, and deletes
       event.user in beforeSend. IF THAT CHANGES, FLIP Linked TO true HERE.

	     NSPrivacyTracking stays false and every Tracking flag below is false:
	     nothing here is shared with a data broker or used for cross-app ads
	     (tracesSampleRate 0, no ad SDK, no ATT prompt).

	     REVIEW THIS FILE whenever a data-touching dependency is added.
	     ================================================================ -->
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
